From 1e58e538021bc456b3d01da9eab63b52c79bdb75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:53:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(front): decline an operator TLC's own Java class
 replaces in a module of the user's

TLC loads its own Java class named after each module of the spec,
wherever the module's text comes from, and runs each public static
method in place of the operator of that module spelled the same,
whatever its arity (processModuleOverrides, for the classes
BuiltInModuleHelper counts as its own). The front end gave an imported
module named like a standard module the builtins of the same names and
arities, and read any other operator by its body: a user's
TransitiveClosure.tla printed its Warshall body where TLC computes the
transitive closure, 264 wrong runs of the upstream conformance suite. A
spec that names such an operator now declines; fallback.md lists the
five runs that matched only by comparing two stub values.
